<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>AI-powered Experiences — UXGyan</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="project-styles.css"></head><body><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="../">UXGyan<span>.</span></a><nav class="nav"><a href="../#work">All projects</a><a href="../about.html">About</a><a href="mailto:gyanart@gmail.com">Contact ↗</a></nav></header><main><section class="case-hero"><p class="case-kicker">03 / AI · PRODUCT STRATEGY · INTERACTION DESIGN</p><h1>Make AI feel useful, not mysterious.</h1><p class="case-lede">An exploration of human–AI workflows that make intent, progress and next actions understandable while keeping people in control.</p><div class="case-meta"><div><span>ROLE</span><strong>Product design exploration</strong></div><div><span>FOCUS</span><strong>AI interaction · UX strategy</strong></div><div><span>PLATFORM</span><strong>Enterprise workspace</strong></div><div><span>FORMAT</span><strong>Interactive concept</strong></div></div></section><div class="case-visual"><div class="showcase" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e6e1f3,#d4cbea)"><div class="assistant-demo"><div class="assistant-head"><i>✳</i><span>Workspace assistant</span><span style="margin-left:auto;color:#888;font-size:10px">CONCEPT DEMO</span></div><div class="chat-area" id="chat-area"><div class="chat-msg">Hi Gyan. I can help structure a task, explore options and explain the reasoning behind a recommendation. What are you working on?</div></div><div class="prompt-chips"><button data-prompt="Summarise the main UX risks in this workflow.">Summarise UX risks</button><button data-prompt="Help me plan a user research study.">Plan research</button><button data-prompt="Turn these observations into design opportunities.">Find opportunities</button></div><form class="chat-input" id="chat-form"><input id="chat-prompt" placeholder="Ask the assistant to help with a task…" autocomplete="off"><button class="demo-button" type="submit">Send ↑</button></form></div></div></div><section class="case-section"><p class="case-label">DESIGN PRINCIPLES</p><h2>Trust is designed into the workflow.</h2><p>Useful AI experiences make it clear what the system understood, what it is doing, what information it used and where a person can intervene. The assistant above is a local interaction prototype with scripted responses; it is not connected to an AI model or external data.</p><div class="case-grid"><article class="case-tile"><b>Visible intent</b><p>Reflect the user's request before taking consequential action.</p></article><article class="case-tile"><b>Explainable progress</b><p>Show meaningful steps, sources and uncertainty rather than a black-box spinner.</p></article><article class="case-tile"><b>Human control</b><p>Make review, correction, undo and escalation part of the primary flow.</p></article></div></section><section class="case-section"><p class="case-label">INTERACTION TO EXPLORE</p><h2>Start with a task, not a chat box.</h2><p>Try one of the suggested prompts or enter your own. The prototype demonstrates conversational states and prompt entry; the next design iteration should test task-specific flows, confirmation points and recovery from incorrect outputs.</p></section></main><div class="case-next"><span>NEXT PROJECT</span><a href="design-systems.html">Enterprise design systems ↗</a></div><footer class="case-footer"><a href="../">UXGyan.</a><span>AI interaction concept</span><a href="../#work">All projects ↑</a></footer><script src="project.js"></script></body></html>